<title>SOUTH AFRICA: HomeChoice year earnings surges.</title>
<headline>HomeChoice year earnings surges.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Headline earnings     14.1	  vs  4.6</p>
<p>    Net after tax income  11.62	 vs  3.54</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   17.97	 vs  5.58</p>
<p>    Tax			  6.35	 vs  2.04</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    3.85	 vs  2.85</p>
<p>    Turnover		 142.11	 vs 92.88</p>
<p>Full name: HomeChoice (direct marketing)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group, which was listed last year, said it would pay its maiden dividend when it released its interim results for the current financial year.</p>
<p>It said customer demand remained strong and it was confident that its forecast of a turnover of 170 million rand and earnings per share of 17.5 cents for 1997 would be exceeded.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
